    descriptionEn: "Gulai Cancang is a traditional ceremonial curry always present at Minangkabau wedding feasts (baralek) and major cultural celebrations. The name 'Cancang' refers to the distinctive fine dicing technique of the meat into small cubes.\n\nThe main ingredients are beef or mutton finely diced into small cubes (including rib cartilage, fat, and bone marrow), slow-cooked in thick coconut milk with ground red chili paste, shallots, garlic, galangal, ginger, star anise, cinnamon, cardamom, nutmeg, and toasted coconut paste (ambu-ambu).\n\nThe hallmark of Gulai Cancang is its small bite-sized meat cubes and a glistening deep red layer of spiced coconut oil floating atop the curry. Its fiery, oily, and deeply complex spice profile makes it a cherished favorite at every traditional celebration.",
