    descriptionEn: "Gulai Tunjang showcases the Minangkabau philosophy of total livestock utilization without waste. The main ingredient is cow foot tendons and surrounding skin/cartilage (tunjang/kikil) boiled for hours until gelatinously tender.\n\nOnce soft, the tendons are slow-cooked in thick coconut milk curry with chilies, turmeric, galangal, lemongrass, kaffir lime leaves, garlic, shallots, and asam kandis. The extended slow-cooking process transforms the tendons into an incredibly soft, chewy, gelatin-clear texture.\n\nThe silky-smooth gelatin texture absorbs the spiced curry broth perfectly after hours of low-heat simmering. Rich in natural collagen, Gulai Tunjang remains a beloved staple at every Padang restaurant.",
