    descriptionEn: "Pinyaram is a traditional Minangkabau sweet cake from Tanah Datar and Kayu Tanam (Padang Pariaman). This delicacy is an essential offering at major Minang ceremonies including manjapuik marapulai weddings, clan chief inaugurations (batagak penghulu), and Eid celebrations.\n\nThe ingredients are simple yet produce extraordinary flavors: fermented white or black glutinous rice flour, melted palm sugar (brown sugar), and coconut milk. Each piece is individually fried in small round wok pans until forming crispy lacy ruffled outer edges with a thick, dense, and soft-chewy center.\n\nThe deep caramel sweetness of palm sugar blends with savory coconut aroma, creating a delightful treat perfect alongside hot tea. Pinyaram symbolizes sweet blessings, prosperity, and Minangkabau cultural hospitality.",
